{"data": [{"author_id": "21347707", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421744634142984"], "id": "2117421744634142984", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg One pattern I've seen is that safeguards work best when they're built into the normal way work gets done. \n\nPreventing a problem before deployment is far more dependable than relying entirely on people to catch it afterward. ✨", "url": "https://x.com/JeffJamesMartin/status/2117421744634142984"}, {"author_id": "1656168114978017281", "created_at": "2026-11-03T01:00:55.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117421731698954696"], "id": "2117421731698954696", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking a hijacked package before it ships beats any clean-up after. Quietly vital work.", "url": "https://x.com/ucdops/status/2117421731698954696"}, {"author_id": "1466030314019504137", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:04:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117407486261047369"], "id": "2117407486261047369", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking the deployment is a useful backstop. Showing which dependency triggered it would make the next step a lot less of a guessing game.", "url": "https://x.com/AleksejAros/status/2117407486261047369"}, {"author_id": "1330209814790746114", "created_at": "2026-11-03T00:03:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117407211294974287"], "id": "2117407211294974287", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117406375219196117", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg https://t.co/W84xiFzgPw", "url": "https://x.com/brookservers/status/2117407211294974287"}, {"author_id": "922414090026446848", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:53:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117404780989431873"], "id": "2117404780989431873", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "quoted"}, {"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking at deploy is the right place. Same rule for agents: a dependency or tool can be hijacked, so check what leaves. RAN: a plan check that blocks \"read config, send it out.\" PLANNED: scanning output before it leaves.\n\nhttps://t.co/YyEixq8NKk\n\nSource: https://t.co/LlvRUdnaUK https://t.co/71jkabqrZr", "url": "https://x.com/Mickey1is2Much/status/2117404780989431873"}, {"author_id": "1369392763394023427", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:37:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117400822028091671"], "id": "2117400822028091671", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Gate placement is the whole thing. In my setup credentials are minted per job, scoped to the task, and permission gates block destructive calls in code before they run. A block at deploy still leaves the install script that already ran on a laptop or in CI with whatever it could", "url": "https://x.com/K0iaK0ia/status/2117400822028091671"}, {"author_id": "15540222", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:13:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117394673555902917"], "id": "2117394673555902917", "in_reply_to_user_id": "1485641965681131540", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 109, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117393813186519429", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@drefrajo yes although we look forward to extending this to other ecosystems (like python which had its supply chain heyday with litellm again)", "url": "https://x.com/rauchg/status/2117394673555902917"}, {"author_id": "1485641965681131540", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:09:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117393813186519429"], "id": "2117393813186519429", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 41, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg though interestingly we didn't see a lot of dramatic npm incidents in the last few weeks", "url": "https://x.com/drefrajo/status/2117393813186519429"}, {"author_id": "1992461", "created_at": "2026-11-02T23:02:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117391821173370918"], "id": "2117391821173370918", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 4, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking at deploy time is the right backstop, but the real exfil window is earlier: a hijacked package's preinstall/postinstall script runs arbitrary code the moment a dev types `npm install` locally, with their SSH keys and .env in reach. Deployment gating never sees that.", "url": "https://x.com/fishjar/status/2117391821173370918"}, {"author_id": "2030403383115595776", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:58:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117390968253260029"], "id": "2117390968253260029", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Somewhere a `postinstall` script just found out it's been let go.", "url": "https://x.com/geekcheats/status/2117390968253260029"}, {"author_id": "915955480585015298", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:33:20.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117384593539997980"], "id": "2117384593539997980", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg The other exfil path is your own laptop, where a postinstall script or a coding agent can just read plaintext .env. I built hush, a small tool which keeps real API keys out of the agent's view.", "url": "https://x.com/MattMarras/status/2117384593539997980"}, {"author_id": "2096242325748125696", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:28:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117383457135354358"], "id": "2117383457135354358", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg nice. other half is what the build can reach if a bad package does run. shouldn't find prod keys sitting in env vars. scoped deploy tokens per project cut the blast radius a lot", "url": "https://x.com/orionxaus/status/2117383457135354358"}, {"author_id": "2045518207159525376", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:19:18.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117381058391900554"], "id": "2117381058391900554", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking before install scripts run is the key. Once it executes, you are already rotating secrets.", "url": "https://x.com/i_mika_el/status/2117381058391900554"}, {"author_id": "1184383192058519552", "created_at": "2026-11-02T22:06:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117377830057394367"], "id": "2117377830057394367", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 28, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Is npm install in Sandbox covered here?", "url": "https://x.com/dschewchenko/status/2117377830057394367"}, {"author_id": "1626696833673187345", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:30:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117368715797049453"], "id": "2117368715797049453", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 21, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg does it catch bad ones already sitting in a lockfile too, or just new installs?", "url": "https://x.com/MarkockiAdam/status/2117368715797049453"}, {"author_id": "2105900716254781440", "created_at": "2026-11-02T21:06:34.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117362755581723081"], "id": "2117362755581723081", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Thank you, and I really appreciate the hard work of @vercel and its team for giving us open-source projects.", "url": "https://x.com/fahadali_yt/status/2117362755581723081"}, {"author_id": "257157930", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:58:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117360658450686214"], "id": "2117360658450686214", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 27, "like_count": 1, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Needed this tbh, feels like theres a hijacked npm package every week now", "url": "https://x.com/JonsTechYT/status/2117360658450686214"}, {"author_id": "378292434", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:53:36.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117359493474607549"], "id": "2117359493474607549", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking at deploy is the right choke point since by then the bad version is already in the lockfile\n\nThe other cheap guard is a cooldown that refuses packages published in the last day or two, since hijacks tend to get caught fast", "url": "https://x.com/Bijan_Automates/status/2117359493474607549"}, {"author_id": "2054501072966684672", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:44:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117357207981588954"], "id": "2117357207981588954", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Blocking a version doesn't clean trees that already installed it. node_modules and the npm cache survive a rebuild, so force a re-resolve, not a redeploy.", "url": "https://x.com/TinyRouterHQ/status/2117357207981588954"}, {"author_id": "1160064457546113026", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:39:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117355941033120029"], "id": "2117355941033120029", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg a heads up showing exactly which package got blocked would be gold", "url": "https://x.com/uiNerd/status/2117355941033120029"}, {"author_id": "2102318912625094656", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:38:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117355575134896198"], "id": "2117355575134896198", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg The tough part is the detection window before an advisory goes public. Does this rely on static analysis of install scripts, or mostly threat feed matching?", "url": "https://x.com/JohnKocdr/status/2117355575134896198"}, {"author_id": "1649511182384914433", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:24:49.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117352248485564445"], "id": "2117352248485564445", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 6, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg blocking at deploy is great but last september's worst npm attack hit before any deploy\n\nit ran during npm install and took tokens straight from dev laptops and ci", "url": "https://x.com/elijahsystems/status/2117352248485564445"}, {"author_id": "2047608467179888640", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:24:17.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117352113596776754"], "id": "2117352113596776754", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 7, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg wait \ndoes it catch ones already sitting in the lockfile or only fresh installs", "url": "https://x.com/theozbuilds/status/2117352113596776754"}, {"author_id": "2108659715039166464", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:22:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117351664520765630"], "id": "2117351664520765630", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg npm install is still the one command where running strangers' code is the feature", "url": "https://x.com/theproductop/status/2117351664520765630"}, {"author_id": "2102899240481542144", "created_at": "2026-11-02T20:16:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2117350069406253531"], "id": "2117350069406253531", "in_reply_to_user_id": "15540222", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 61, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2117328043228471552", "type": "replied_to"}], "text": "@rauchg Good, my agent has been running npm install like it's free samples at Costco", "url": "https://x.com/ShlomoFaig/status/2117350069406253531"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "21347707", "name": "Jeff James Martin", "username": "JeffJamesMartin"}, {"id": "1656168114978017281", "name": "UCDOps", "username": "ucdops"}, {"id": "1466030314019504137", "name": "Alex Yarosh · AI expert · CEO of AI Studio", "username": "AleksejAros"}, {"id": "1330209814790746114", "name": "Brook | flisk.sh", "username": "brookservers"}, {"id": "922414090026446848", "name": "ЯR + ML = 4S's", "username": "Mickey1is2Much"}, {"id": "1369392763394023427", "name": "KoiaKoia", "username": "K0iaK0ia"}, {"id": "15540222", "name": "Guillermo Rauch", "username": "rauchg"}, {"id": "1485641965681131540", "name": "drefrajo", "username": "drefrajo"}, {"id": "1992461", "name": "Gabe", "username": "fishjar"}, {"id": "2030403383115595776", "name": "GeekCheats", "username": "geekcheats"}, {"id": "915955480585015298", "name": "Matteo Marras", "username": "MattMarras"}, {"id": "2096242325748125696", "name": "OrionX", "username": "orionxaus"}, {"id": "2045518207159525376", "name": "Mikhail Rogov", "username": "i_mika_el"}, {"id": "1184383192058519552", "name": "Dmytro Shevchenko 🇺🇦", "username": "dschewchenko"}, {"id": "1626696833673187345", "name": "Adam", "username": "MarkockiAdam"}, {"id": "2105900716254781440", "name": "Fahad Ali", "username": "fahadali_yt"}, {"id": "257157930", "name": "JonsTech", "username": "JonsTechYT"}, {"id": "378292434", "name": "Bijan | AI for Law Firms | Investor", "username": "Bijan_Automates"}, {"id": "2054501072966684672", "name": "TinyRouter", "username": "TinyRouterHQ"}, {"id": "1160064457546113026", "name": "Alex Tatu", "username": "uiNerd"}, {"id": "2102318912625094656", "name": "John K", "username": "JohnKocdr"}, {"id": "1649511182384914433", "name": "Elijah｜Systems", "username": "elijahsystems"}, {"id": "2047608467179888640", "name": "Oz Wadood", "username": "theozbuilds"}, {"id": "2108659715039166464", "name": "Product Operator", "username": "theproductop"}, {"id": "2102899240481542144", "name": "Shlomo F.", "username": "ShlomoFaig"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2117421744634142984", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzlyibhfwtvdou06cvwwjoljbdqwt", "oldest_id": "2117350069406253531", "result_count": 25}}